    "result_text": "The build is green \u2014 both acceptance tests pass.\n\n## Summary\n\nI changed the locality derivation to prefer the postcode over the city.\n\n**`LocalityDeriver.java`** \u2014 added a two-arg `locality(String city, String postcode)` that:\n1. First looks up the region by postcode range (`regionForPostcode`): NSW 2000\u20132099, VIC 3000\u20133099, QLD 4000\u20134099.\n2. Falls back to the existing city-to-region table only when the postcode is absent, not a 4-digit value, or in no known range.\n\nThe original single-arg `locality(String city)` is kept intact \u2014 it's still used by `OwnerRestControllerV1.validatePostcode` to validate a postcode against the *city's* region, which is a separate concern from display derivation.\n\n**`OwnerMapper.java`** \u2014 updated the `locality` mapping expression to pass the postcode through:\n`LocalityDeriver.locality(owner.getCity(), owner.getPostcode())`.\n\nThis returns the same region for known cities (e.g. Sydney \u2192 NSW) but now disambiguates via postcode \u2014 e.g. an unknown city with postcode 3000 resolves to VIC, as the new `functionalityPostcodePreferredOverCity` test asserts.\n\n`Tests run: 2, Failures: 0, Errors: 0` \u2014 BUILD SUCCESS.",
