    "probe_text": "Here is the complete, in-order list of everything that happens when you `POST /api/owners`. The handler is `OwnerRestControllerV1.addOwner` (`src/main/java/org/springframework/samples/petclinic/rest/controller/v1/OwnerRestControllerV1.java:129`), binding the body to `OwnerFieldsDto` via `@Valid @RequestBody`.\n\n## Authorization (only if enabled)\n- **`@PreAuthorize(\"hasRole(@roles.OWNER_ADMIN)\")`** \u2014 requires `ROLE_OWNER_ADMIN`. **But by default it is NOT enforced**: `petclinic.security.enable=false` (`application.properties:49`) activates `DisableSecurityConfig` (`permitAll`), and method security is only turned on when that property is `true`. So out of the box the endpoint is open.\n\n## Validations (in execution order)\n\n1. **Bean Validation on the DTO** (`@Valid`, before the method body) \u2014 fails \u2192 `400`:\n   - `firstName`: `@NotNull`, `@Size(1..30)`, `@Pattern` `^[\\p{L}]+([ '-][\\p{L}]+){0,2}$`\n   - `lastName`: `@NotNull`, `@Size(1..30)`, `@Pattern` `^[\\p{L}]+([ '-][\\p{L}]+){0,2}\\.?$`\n   - `address`: `@NotNull`, `@Size(1..255)`\n   - `city`: `@NotNull`, `@Size(1..80)`\n   - `telephone`: `@NotNull`, `@Size(1..20)`\n   - `email` (optional): `@Size(1..255)`, `@Email`\n   - `postcode` (optional): `@Pattern` `^[0-9]{4}$`, `@Size(4..4)`\n\n2. **Manual required-field check** \u2014 collects blanks among `firstName`, `lastName`, normalized `address`, `city`, `telephone`; if any \u2192 `MissingOwnerFieldsException` \u2192 `400`.\n\n3. **Postcode validation** (`validatePostcode`) \u2014 if present, must be 4 digits and, when the city's region is known (NSW/VIC/QLD), fall in that region's range (2000\u20132099 / 3000\u20133099 / 4000\u20134099) \u2192 else `InvalidPostcodeException` \u2192 `400`.\n\n4. **Daily registration limit** \u2014 resolves the registration date to a business day, counts existing owners already registered that day; if `>= 100` \u2192 `DailyRegistrationLimitException` \u2192 `429`.\n\n5. **City capacity** \u2014 counts existing owners in the same city (case-insensitive); if `>= 50` \u2192 `CityAtCapacityException` \u2192 `409`.\n\n6. **Telephone E.164 normalization** (`toE164`) \u2014 strips formatting, applies `+61` default / national-length rules (8\u201315 digits; `+61`\u21929, `+1`\u219210); invalid \u2192 `InvalidTelephoneException` \u2192 `400`.\n\n7. **Email normalization** (`normalizeEmail`) \u2014 blank \u2192 null; otherwise must match the email pattern \u2192 else `InvalidEmailException` \u2192 `400`.\n\n8. **Duplicate identity check** \u2014 computes `identityKey = telephone|email|householdId` and scans all owners; if a match exists \u2192 `DuplicateIdentityException` \u2192 `409`.\n\n9. **Entity-level (on persist)** \u2014 Hibernate re-validates the `Owner` entity: `@NotEmpty` on firstName/lastName/address/city/telephone and `@Pattern ^\\+[0-9]{8,15}$` on telephone (the E.164 output is built to satisfy this).\n\n## Side-effects (in execution order)\n\n1. **Address is normalized and written back** onto the DTO (trim, collapse whitespace, upper-case, expand `ST\u2192STREET`, `RD\u2192ROAD`, `AVE\u2192AVENUE`).\n2. A `bulkSignupWarning` flag is set when the day's registrations `> 80`.\n3. **Household detection + backfill** \u2014 finds existing owners with the same normalized last name + address; if any, computes a deterministic `householdId` and, for each member missing/differing on it, **updates and re-saves that existing owner** (extra writes to other records).\n4. **Telephone written back** to the DTO in E.164 form.\n5. **Email written back** to the DTO (trimmed, lower-cased, or null).\n6. DTO \u2192 `Owner` entity via MapStruct (`toOwner`), then explicit fields set on the new owner:\n   - `registrationDate` = resolved business day (defaults to today, rolled off weekends).\n   - `customerCode` = `\"<CITY3>-<LAST3>-<NNNN>\"` where NNNN = (owners in that city)+1, zero-padded.\n   - `householdId` (from step 3, or null).\n   - `namesakeCount` = count of existing owners with the same first+last name.\n   - `bulkSignupWarning` (from step 2).\n   - `householdSize` = existing household members + 1.\n7. **Owner is persisted** (`clinicService.saveOwner`).\n8. **AUDIT log line** emitted (`AUDIT` SLF4J logger): id, customerCode, registrationDate, membershipLevel.\n9. **Response**: entity mapped to `OwnerDto` (with derived read-only fields like `displayName`, `membershipLevel`, `identityKey`), a `Location` header (`/api/owners/{id}`) set, and `201 Created` returned.\n\n## Notes worth flagging\n- **`sharesHousehold` in the DTO is dead input** \u2014 it is never read in the create path; duplicate acceptance is governed solely by the identity-key check.\n- **No JPA lifecycle callbacks, no auditing (`@CreatedDate`/`@CreatedBy`), and no event publishing** occur \u2014 the only non-persistence side effect is the AUDIT log line.\n- `findAllOwners()` is scanned in-memory ~5 times per create; the limit/duplicate checks are **not atomic** with the save.\n- Handlers for `DuplicateTelephoneException`/`DuplicateEmailException`/`DuplicateHouseholdException` exist but are **unreachable** from this path.\n\nI read the code only and made no changes."
